   Yep. Or rather, all water acts like wet water for the purposes of 
splashing. It seems less reasonable /and/ less interesting to make un/holy
water bless/curse items:

   * Currently, unless I'm mistaken, there's no way to get things wet using
only a potion of holy water, unless you un-holify it first, which unless 
I'm mistaken again, you can only do with non-renewable resources. Which 
seems odd. So this patch introduces a little loophole there.
   * Blessing, like poisoning, seems to me like the sort of thing that 
takes care and/or total submerging. Random splashes have neither property.
   * You might make a case for cursing (because the RNG is evil!), but
hmm...

   What about making all splashed water equally wet, but /also/ allowing
un/holy water to bless/curse items with a low probability independent of
the wetting effect? Would that make thrown holy water too powerful?

